From f61d7b7e7cc3dc1e6fbc9e92c06a402a056465da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: silo-research <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:01:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] gvproxy: add -no-gateway-api

gvproxy serves its HTTP API inside the virtual network, on port 80 of
the gateway. Without a token, any process in the guest can use it to
expose a port of the host on all of its interfaces. With
--api-token-file, the guest must hold the token, which means placing it
in the guest and keeping it from the guest's own untrusted processes.

Many users never call the API from the guest: they drive gvproxy from
the host, through --listen or --services. For them the simplest safe
setting is not to serve it inside the network at all.

-no-gateway-api, or `no-gateway-api: true` in the configuration file,
skips the listener on the gateway's port 80. -listen and -services are
unchanged, and so are the DNS server and every forward.
---
 README.md                  |   3 +++
 cmd/gvproxy/config.go      |   6 ++++++
 cmd/gvproxy/config_test.go |  23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 cmd/gvproxy/main.go        |  12 ++++++++----
 4 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 6b6f1d26..72d3ec8e 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -138,6 +138,9 @@ The gateway API endpoint (accessible from the VM at http://192.168.127.1:80) can
 authentication. When enabled, all requests from within the VM require an `Authorization` header
 with the token.
 
+When nothing in the VM needs the API, `--no-gateway-api` stops serving it on the gateway
+address altogether. The API stays available on the host through `--listen` and `--services`.
+
 **Note:** Authentication only applies to the gateway endpoint accessible from the VM. Host-side endpoints
 (`--listen` or `--services`) remain unauthenticated. If they are backed by unix socket, they will be protected by
 the socket file permissions. If you use these with a `tcp` endpoint, they will be unauthenticated even if they would benefit from Bearer token authentication.
diff --git a/cmd/gvproxy/config.go b/cmd/gvproxy/config.go
index 5523fcb3..b9ca10eb 100644
--- a/cmd/gvproxy/config.go
+++ b/cmd/gvproxy/config.go
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@ type GvproxyArgs struct {
 	servicesEndpoint   string
 	ec2MetadataAccess  bool
 	apiTokenFile       string
